            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="KIP01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <forename>Andrew</forename>
                        <surname>Kippis</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1725-03-28">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1795-10-08"/>
                    <occupation>Presbyterian minister</occupation>
                    <occupation>biographer</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">

Kippis was minister of the Presbyterian congregation 
meeting in Princes Street, Westminster from 1753 until his death and one of Godwin's tutors at Hoxton
dissenting college. Extensively discussed by all the biographies, esp. Marshall, who writes that 'of all
his tutors, it was undoubtedly Andrew Kippis who most influenced Godwin at Hoxton' (p. 35). All the 
mentions of Kippis come before Andrew Kippis's death in 1795 and are usually with other dissenters.



</note>
                    <bibl type="printedbook">Marshall</bibl>
                    <bibl type="other">
                        <title>DNB</title>
                    </bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
